---
import { inquiryEmailAddress, inquiryEmailUrl } from "../lib/site";
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="description" content="Design variation: typewritten letter." />
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow" />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#f4f1ea" />
    <title>V1 Typewriter | Modern Faber</title>
    <link rel="icon" type="image/x-icon" href="/favicon.ico" />
    <style is:global>
      * {
        box-sizing: border-box;
        margin: 0;
        padding: 0;
      }

      html {
        background: #f4f1ea;
      }

      body {
        min-height: 100vh;
        max-width: 66ch;
        margin: 0 auto;
        padding: 72px 24px 96px;
        color: #26221b;
        background: #f4f1ea;
        font-family: "Courier New", Courier, ui-monospace, monospace;
        font-size: 15px;
        line-height: 26px;
      }

      main {
        display: grid;
        gap: 26px;
      }

      .letterhead {
        display: grid;
        gap: 4px;
        padding-bottom: 26px;
        border-bottom: 1px solid #26221b;
      }

      h1 {
        font-size: inherit;
        font-weight: 700;
        letter-spacing: 0.35em;
      }

      .dateline {
        letter-spacing: 0.12em;
      }

      .sep {
        text-align: center;
        letter-spacing: 0.6em;
      }

      .salutation {
        font-weight: 700;
      }

      .sig {
        padding-top: 12px;
      }

      a {
        color: inherit;
        text-decoration: underline;
        text-underline-offset: 3px;
      }

      @media (max-width: 600px) {
        body {
          padding: 40px 20px 64px;
        }
      }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <main>
      <header class="letterhead">
        <h1>MODERN FABER</h1>
        <p class="dateline">SUMMER 2026 &middot; NO. 1</p>
      </header>

      <p class="salutation">To the fabers,</p>

      <p>
        Faber is an old word for a maker &mdash; the smith at the forge, the carpenter at the
        bench, the hand that shapes raw material into something that did not exist before.
        <em>Homo faber</em>: the one who makes. There have never been fewer. Not because people
        stopped wanting to make things, but because talking about making became easier than
        making &mdash; the feed rewards the announcement, not the object, and whole rooms fill
        with people circling the work they say they want to do.
      </p>

      <p class="sep" aria-hidden="true">* * *</p>

      <p>
        Modern Faber is a room for the ones who still make. One rule holds it together: come
        back every week with something real, and say what you changed. There is no audience
        here, no applause &mdash; only other fabers paying attention to the details you almost
        skipped. That attention costs something. It is meant to. Keep the rhythm long enough
        and you are left with a body of work, a sharper eye, and the few people you actually
        want beside you at the bench.
      </p>

      <p class="sig">
        Join us: <a href={inquiryEmailUrl}>{inquiryEmailAddress}</a><br />
        &mdash; M.F.
      </p>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
